# Trivy exceptions. Every entry needs the ID, why the risk is accepted, and a review date.
# Policy: security/TRIVY-POLICY.md. Image CVEs are never ignored here.

# AWS-0104 (CRITICAL) EKS node security group allows egress to 0.0.0.0/0.
# Why accepted: worker nodes must reach ECR/GHCR, the EKS API and AWS service
# endpoints through the NAT gateway; the rule comes from the upstream EKS module.
# Mitigation: nodes sit in private subnets with no inbound internet route, IMDSv2
# hop limit 1, and VPC flow logs. Production follow-up: VPC endpoints + an egress
# firewall/allow-list. Review: 2027-01-31.
AWS-0104
